BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tai Chi with Drew
DTSTART;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260720T171500
DTEND;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260720T181500
UID:aa6f6e6049d0debff6c794f117084ca6@wellnesscollectivemoab.com
DESCRIPTION:Among all forms of physical activity\, Tai Chi Ch’uan is per
 hap s the most accessible\, convenient\, and economical way to improve bot
 h phy sical health and mental well-being. As Yang Style Tai Chi master Che
 ng Man- Ching once said\, ‘Those who understand the importance of exerci
 se for heal th will find Tai Chi Ch’uan indispensable.’ While Tai Chi 
 may not be easy t o master\, consistent practice will yield results. In th
 is class\, we wi ll focus on cultivating chi\, building endurance and stre
 ngth\, and develop ing core alignment\, all while learning to release tens
 ion. Tai Chi trainin g offers many levels of progression. In Yang Style\, 
 when practiced correct ly\, it becomes an aerobic workout\, despite minima
 l movement. Additionally \, it serves as a form of meditation. Please wear
  comfortable clothing. Flat shoes\, socks\, or bare feet are ideal. Studen
 ts are encouraged to tra in at their own pace\, and progression will vary 
 from person to person.
LOCATION:Wellness Collective\, 76 S 100 W\, Moab\, UT 84532
X-SOURCE:Wellness Collective Moab
END:VEVENT
