BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Qi-Gong with Cody
DTSTART;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260801T080000
DTEND;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260801T090000
UID:23aea475729ce06096411e74bb115692@wellnesscollectivemoab.com
DESCRIPTION:Zhineng Qigong is a powerful mind-body practice rooted in anci
 e nt Chinese healing traditions and adapted for modern times. This gentle 
 yet profound system blends slow movement\, sound\, visualization\, and med
 itat ion to help individuals cultivate inner peace\, restore balance\, and
  enhan ce vitality. By consciously connecting with the energy of life—wh
 at some ma y call qi or universal life force—participants are invited in
 to a process o f holistic healing: physically\, emotionally\, and spiritua
 lly. One of the most accessible forms of Qigong\, Zhineng emphasizes conne
 ction over comple xity. Its principles can be embraced by people of all ag
 es\, backgrounds\, and physical abilities. Cody teaches from a place of li
 ved experience\, hav ing found this practice deeply healing and transforma
 tive in his own journe y. His classes focus on cultivating shared energy t
 hrough group practice\, empowering individuals to tap into their innate wi
 sdom and live with greate r purpose and presence.
LOCATION:Wellness Collective\, 76 S 100 W\, Moab\, UT 84532
X-SOURCE:Wellness Collective Moab
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Chair Yoga with Breann
DTSTART;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260803T090000
DTEND;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260803T100000
UID:80587dda387fc73b15ac872100bfc909@wellnesscollectivemoab.com
DESCRIPTION:Chair Yoga – Mondays at 9 AM Join us every Monday morning at
  9:00 AM for a gentle and accessible Chair Yoga class\, led by Breann\, a 
 ce rtified trauma-sensitive yoga teacher and experienced massage therapist
 . Breann brings over 20 years of experience in guiding others toward great
 er body awareness\, healing\, and relaxation. This class is designed for e
 very one – whether you are new to yoga\, have limited mobility\, or are 
 looking for a mindful and soothing way to start your week. Chair Yoga allo
 ws you to experience the benefits of yoga without needing to get down on a
  mat. Wha t to Expect: • Seated and standing postures using the chair fo
 r support • G entle stretches to enhance flexibility • Breathing exerc
 ises to calm the mi nd and body • Movements to promote better circulatio
 n and balance ✨ No exp erience necessary – come as you are! Where: Wel
 lness Collective When: Ever y Monday at 9:00 AM Cost: By donation Let this
  practice be a moment of sel f-care and grounding in your week.
LOCATION:Wellness Collective\, 76 S 100 W\, Moab\, UT 84532
X-SOURCE:Wellness Collective Moab
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tai Chi with Drew
DTSTART;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260803T171500
DTEND;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260803T181500
UID:1413fa70f5523e52adf6a1827666aee0@wellnesscollectivemoab.com
DESCRIPTION:Among all forms of physical activity\, Tai Chi Ch’uan is per
 hap s the most accessible\, convenient\, and economical way to improve bot
 h phy sical health and mental well-being. As Yang Style Tai Chi master Che
 ng Man- Ching once said\, ‘Those who understand the importance of exerci
 se for heal th will find Tai Chi Ch’uan indispensable.’ While Tai Chi 
 may not be easy t o master\, consistent practice will yield results. In th
 is class\, we wi ll focus on cultivating chi\, building endurance and stre
 ngth\, and develop ing core alignment\, all while learning to release tens
 ion. Tai Chi trainin g offers many levels of progression. In Yang Style\, 
 when practiced correct ly\, it becomes an aerobic workout\, despite minima
 l movement. Additionally \, it serves as a form of meditation. Please wear
  comfortable clothing. Flat shoes\, socks\, or bare feet are ideal. Studen
 ts are encouraged to tra in at their own pace\, and progression will vary 
 from person to person.
LOCATION:Wellness Collective\, 76 S 100 W\, Moab\, UT 84532
X-SOURCE:Wellness Collective Moab
END:VEVENT
